PART 2  SCREEN OF SWITCH CLASSES (cheap symbolic checks; the reasoning is in the README table)
==============================================================================================================
  S1: d(1/K')/dX = -Derivative(Kp(X), X)/Kp(X)**2  (< 0 when K'' > 0: screened at large X)
  S2: standard broken branch phi^2 = [] (exists only for rho < mu^2 M^2: OFF in dense)
      inverted broken branch phi^2 = [] (exists only for rho > mu^2 M^2: ON in dense) -> carried to Part 3
  S3: discriminant 4*c*s + 1; c<0 branch has no real root for s > -1/(4*c); Z = 2*c*x + 1 -> 0 at x = -1/(2*c) (s = -1/(4*c)): strong coupling at the threshold; c>0 branch: x ~ sqrt(s/c), suppression (Vainshtein, wrong direction)
  S4: d2(-B W(P/rho))/dP^2 = -B*Subs(Derivative(W(_xi_1), (_xi_1, 2)), _xi_1, p/rho)/rho**2  (sign of -W'': negative where W''>0 -> negative thermal stiffness, N14)
  S5: d/dx_i <rho_b>_leaf(tau) = 0  (cannot localise)

