PART 3  THE CANDIDATE: QUADRATIC ACTIONS (sympy)
==============================================================================================================
  broken phase: sigma_bar^2 = 2*B/mu0**2 + mu0**2/lambda - mu0**2/(lambda*Ufun(rho))   (= v^2 (T + 2/R), R = E_c/B, E_c = mu0^2 v^2)
  M^2 (broken) = 4*B*lambda/mu0**2 + 2*mu0**2 - 2*mu0**2/Ufun(rho)  -> 2 lambda sigma_bar^2 > 0 wherever the broken phase exists
  M^2 (symmetric, sigma = 0) = -2*B*lambda/mu0**2 - mu0**2 + mu0**2/Ufun(rho)  -> > 0 iff T < -2/R (OFF side)
  FRW / OFF side: g_x = 0, E_dir = 0, df/dsigma = 0, f = 0

